    "created_at": "2015-09-06T00:42:03Z",
    "updated_at": "2015-09-06T00:42:03Z",
    "body": "> Once whatwg/html-build#15 lands and we can have a separate cache and temp folders, I don't see any reason anything should be dot-prefixed.\n\nOK, yeah, true—I hadn’t hacked up the cache-dir part yet, but I will now.\n\nSo that leads to a question: Which one of the following do we have the build script do?\n\nA. Copy the `source` file into the cache dir.\nB. Reference the path to the existing repo `source` file.\n\nIf we do **A**, the we don’t need to change the filenames in the BOILERPLATE includes in the spec, and we can just close this PR.\n\nBut if we do **B**, then we still need to change the filenames; it’s just that we need to instead change them to, e.g., `<!--BOILERPLATE cache/entities.inc-->` (assuming we name the cache dir \"`cache`\"). Right?\n\nIMHO it would be better to do just have the build script (continue to) reference the path to the existing repo `source` file, and so do **B**. Adding a copy step is just one more operation that can fail (however unlikely it is that will ever fail, given its simplicity).\n\nBut I’m glad to write it up either way. Just lemme know which you think we should do.\n",
